WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.900
Are you a SMART fella,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.933
or a FART smella?

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.433
Let's find OUT!

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.500
Check this out,

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.433
a word analogy!

00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:13.967
King is to queen,

00:00:13.967 --> 00:00:16.533
as prince is to...

00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:17.167
what?

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:17.800
A.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:18.433
Crown,

00:00:18.433 --> 00:00:19.067
B.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:19.700
Castle,

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:20.333
C.

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:20.967
Royal,

00:00:20.967 --> 00:00:22.233
or D.

00:00:22.233 --> 00:00:22.900
Princess?

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.167
Five seconds!

00:00:29.933 --> 00:00:31.133
TIME'S UP!

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.233
It's...

00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:32.667
D,

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:33.067
princess!

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:35.633
A king and queen are the

00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:37.333
male and female pair,

00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:39.900
so the female of a prince

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.167
is a princess.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:42.967
Okay,

00:00:42.967 --> 00:00:45.000
a number series!

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.667
Two,

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:46.333
four,

00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:47.000
seven,

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:47.667
eleven,

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:48.333
sixteen,

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:49.700
and then...

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.700
what comes next?

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.367
A.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:53.067
Twenty-one,

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:53.733
B.

00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:54.400
Twenty,

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.067
C.

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:55.733
Twenty-three,

00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:57.100
or D.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:57.767
Twenty-two?

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:59.100
Five seconds!

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.100
TIME'S UP!

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.567
The answer is...

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:09.167
D,

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:09.767
twenty-two!

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:12.733
The gaps grow by one:

00:01:12.733 --> 00:01:13.933
plus two,

00:01:13.933 --> 00:01:14.533
three,

00:01:14.533 --> 00:01:15.133
four,

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:15.733
five,

00:01:15.733 --> 00:01:17.500
then plus six.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.100
So sixteen plus six is twenty-two.

00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:23.233
Here's one,

00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:24.767
a shape puzzle!

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:26.800
Which shape comes next?

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:27.300
A.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.300
A circle,

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:28.833
B.

00:01:28.833 --> 00:01:29.833
A hexagon,

00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:30.333
C.

00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:31.367
A heptagon,

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:32.367
or D.

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:33.367
An octagon?

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:34.400
Five seconds!

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.367
TIME'S UP!

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:43.633
The answer is...

00:01:43.633 --> 00:01:44.167
C,

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.200
a heptagon!

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.400
The sides count up by one:

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.433
square four,

00:01:49.433 --> 00:01:50.500
pentagon five,

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.567
hexagon six,

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:54.733
so next is the heptagon with

00:01:54.733 --> 00:01:55.800
seven sides.

00:01:56.933 --> 00:01:57.333
So,

00:01:57.333 --> 00:01:59.367
are you smart or fart?

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:01.800
Count up your correct answers to

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.000
find your rank!

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:04.500
So,

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.900
how did you do?

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.267
Comment your score below,

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:08.633
and follow for more!
